The attached image demonstrates Nano-11's ability to improve antigen targeting to immunopotentiating cells in draining lymph nodes and enhance antigen retention at the injection site. Panel A shows that migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) exhibit the highest expression of CD86 among OVA+ cells in the lymph node, highlighting their activation status. Panel B further characterizes these OVA+ and OVA- MigDCs by CD11b and Ly6C expression, indicating distinct myeloid cell populations involved. Panel C, using in vivo fluorescence imaging, illustrates that Nano-11, similar to aluminum hydroxide adjuvant (AH), effectively retains Alexa Fluor 647-conjugated OVA at the injection site for at least 7 days, whereas soluble OVA rapidly clears, confirming Nano-11's role in prolonged antigen presentation.